      "id": "PRP-01",
      "chapter": "inputs",
      "title": "Two progressions and their host quantifiers",
      "anchor": "inputs-prime-pair",
      "statement": "For each M>0, 0<ε<1/52 and A≥1, all sufficiently large Y admit q,d in the prescribed logarithmic ranges and congruence classes. In the host proof M=ψ.N and A=J. The same pair must pass every indicated analytic test.",
      "hypotheses": "Both stages have a nonempty population with the common thresholds described below. The congruence product is odd and q is an odd prime.",
