        "quadratic Jacobi twist",
        "primitive inducing character",
        "zero-free box",
        "Chinese remainder theorem"
      ],
      "equations": [],
      "dependencies": [],
      "correspondence": "With z=Y^(ε/5), z′=z(log Y)^2, take q≡3 mod 8 and d≡7 mod 16, d≡−1 mod q∏_{3≤p≤z}p. The second modulus describes one reduced residue class. Example z=3,q=11,d=263 is solely a check of the congruences.",
